  "readmeFile": "README.nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "17.3.1: Fixes an unattended install or upgrade failing with \"no such table: umbracoAIEvaluationCache\" when another package publishes content during install (issue #25). Cache clean-up on publish/unpublish now waits until Umbraco is fully running and never blocks a publish. 17.3.0: Requires Umbraco CMS 17.6.2+ and Umbraco.AI 17.3.4+ (UUI 2, EF Core 10.0.10). Language-aware evaluation, recommendations, Apply and per-language caching on multilingual sites. Rich Text recommendations can be applied directly, with a safeguard that withholds Apply when embedded blocks would be lost, and now always come back as clean HTML (previously they could be returned in the editor's internal JSON format). Provider-enforced JSON response schemas with an automatic fallback. A notice when the AI model ignores the deterministic (temperature) setting. Localized messages for aborted/timed-out AI requests and for gateway timeouts/unreachable gateways. Evaluation cache is migrated automatically on first start. Installing on a site older than Umbraco 17.6.2 now fails with a clear NU1605 error instead of partially upgrading the CMS.",
